<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115360" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψᾱρός</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψάρ</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>like a starling,</i> i.
			e. <i>speckled, dappled,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψ. ἵππος</span> a <i>dapple-grey</i>
			horse, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1225
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Za.</u>
				1.8
			</span></i>; <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				632b19
			</span></i> distinguishes it fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποικίλος,</span> which implies that the spots are more
			distinctly marked:—
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψαρότερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					12.28
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				11.11
			</span></i>.</div>
